hadiths[56]{hadithnumber,text}:
"156","'Ali ibn Talib reported that when the illness of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, deepened, he said, \'Ali! Bring me a page on which I can write something for my community after which they will not go astray."" 'Ali said"
"157","'Abdullah reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Respond to invitations. Do not reject gifts. Do not beat Muslims."""
"158","'Ali reported that the last words of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, were:The prayer! The prayer! Fear Allah concerning your slaves!"""
"159","Abu'd-Darda' used to say to people. We know you better than the veterinarian knows his animals. We recognise the best of you from the worst of you. The best of you is the one whose good is hoped for and the one whose evil you are safe from. As for the worst of you"
"160","Abu Umama said, Ingratitude is typified by someone who refuses to give"
"161","Al-Hasan reported that a man ordered one of his slaves to draw water using one of his camels and the man fell asleep. The master came with a torch and put it in his face and the slave fell into the well. In the morning, the slave went to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'Umar saw what had happened to his slave and therefore 'Umar set him free.""162"""
"162","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Amrah, from Amrah, that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) had granted a slave-girl her freedom (tadbir). Then Aisha fell ill, so her nephews asked a physician from the Zutt. He said: ""You are informing me about a bewitched woman; a slave-girl of hers bewitched her."" Aisha was informed. She said: ""You bewitched me?"" She said: ""Yes."" She said: ""Why? You will never succeed."" Then she said: ""Sell her to the worst of the Arabs as a slave."""
"163","He narrated to us Hajjaj, who said: Hammad, the son of Salmah, narrated to us, who said: Abu Ghalib informed us, from Abu Umaymah, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) turned back with two boys, and one of them was given to Ali (may God's blessings be upon him), and he said: Do not beat him, for I have been forbidden from beating the inhabitants of the mosque, and I saw him praying since we turned back. He gave Abu Dharr a boy and said: Take care of him well, and he said: What did you do? He said: You ordered me to take care of him well, so I did."
"164","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) came to Medina and did not have a servant. So Abu Talhah took hold of my hand and led me to the Prophet (peace be upon him). I said: ""O Prophet of Allah, Anas is a young, noble, and noble-minded slave. Let him serve you."" I served him on journeys and in the city until he passed away (peace be upon him). He never asked me about anything I did: ""Why did you do this?"" And he never asked me about anything I did not do: ""Why did you not do this?"""
"165","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When a slave steals"
"166","Laqit ibn Sabira reported that his father said, I went to the Prophet"
"167","Abu'l-'Aliyya said, We were ordered to finish off things for the servant and to measure and count because we did not want to allow them to accustom themselves to bad habits nor for anyone to think evil of us."""
"168","Salman said, I count the soup bones for my slave"
"169","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq informed us, saying: I heard Harithah ibn Mudarrib say: I heard Salman: ""I indeed count the Iraqis out of fear of suspicion."""
"170","Yazid ibn 'Abdullah said, \'Abdullah ibn 'Umar sent a slave of his with some gold - or silver - and he changed it and deferred the exchange (i.e. he changed gold into silver or vice versa and did not take the money straightaway. This is haram.) Then he went back to Ibn 'Umar who gave him a painful beating. He said"
"171","Abu Mas'ud said, I was beating a slave of mine when I heard a voice behind me"
"172","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Do not say"
"173","He told us 'Abdullah bin Muhammad, he said: He told us Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Do not say: ""May Allah curse your face and the face of whoever resembles your face,"" for indeed Allah, the Exalted, created Adam, peace be upon him, in His own form."
"174","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When one of you strikes his servant"
"175","He narrated to us Khalid, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) passed by a donkey whose ears had been pierced, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""May Allah curse whoever does this, no one should pierce the ears of a donkey or pierce them."""
"176","Hilal ibn Yasaf said, We used to sell linen in the house of Suwayd ibn Muqarrin. A slavegirl came out and said something to one of the men and that man slapped her. Suwayd ibn Muqarrin asked him"
"177","Ibn 'Umar said, I heard the Prophet"
"178","Mu'awiya ibn Muqarrin said, I slapped a mawla of mine and he fled. Then my father called me and said"
"179","He informed us, Amr ibn Marzooq, he said: Shu'bah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me: What is your name? I said: Shu'bah. He said: Abu Shu'bah informed me, from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani, who saw a man who had beaten his slave, and he said: Did you not know that the image is forbidden? I saw myself, and I am one of seven brothers, during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, we had only a servant, so one of us beat him, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, ordered us to set him free."
"180","Abu 'Umar Zadhan said, We were with Ibn 'Umar when he summoned a slave of his whom he had beaten and he uncovered his back. 'Does it hurt?' he asked. 'No"
"181","'Ammar ibn Yasir said, None of you beats his slave unjustly without the slave receiving retaliation from him on the Day of Rising."""
"182","Abu Layla said, Salman went out and when his animal fodder fell from the manger"
"183","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Give people their rights. Even the hornless sheep will take retaliation from the horned sheep."""
"184","Umm Salama reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was in his house and called for a slave of his (or hers) and she was slow in coming. The anger showed in his face. Umm Salama went to the curtain and found the slavegirl playing. He had a siwak-stick with him and said, 'Were it not that I fear retaliation on the Day of Rising with this siwak."""
"185","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, On the Day of Rising"
"186","Khalifah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Shqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever strikes an unjust blow, retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"187","'Ubada ibn al-Walid said, My father and I went out to seek knowledge from the Ansar in this area before they died. The first one we met was Abu'l-Yasar"
"188","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said, The Prophet"
"189","Al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd said, I saw Abu Dharr wearing a robe and his slave was also wearing a robe. We asked him about that and he said"
"190","Sallam ibn 'Amr reported from one of the Companions of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Your slaves are your brothers"
"191","Abu Hurayra said, 'Help the worker in his work. The one who works for Allah will not be disappointed,\ i.e. the servant."""
"192","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, The slave has his food and clothing. Do not burden a slave with work which he is incapable of doing."""
"193","Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Bukayr, that Ajlan Abu Muhammad narrated to him shortly before his death, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The slave has his food and his clothing, and he should not be burdened except with what he can bear."""
"194","Ma'rur said, We passed by Abu Dharr and he was wearing a garment and his slave had a robe on. We said"
"195","Al-Miqdam heard the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say, What you feed yourself is sadaqa. What you feed your child"
"196","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, The best sadaqa is that which leaves you free of want. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Begin with those you look after. Your wife says"
"197","He told us Muhammad bin Khatib, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Muhammad bin 'Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet ordered charity, so a man said: I have a dinar, he said: Spend it on yourself, he said: I have another, he said: Spend it on your wife, he said: I have another, he said: Spend it on your servant, then you will be blessed."
"198","Ibn Jurayj related that Abu'z-Zubayr heard him ask Jabir about when a man's servant has finished his work and heat (i.e. cooking). Did the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, command that the servant be invited to eat? Yes"
"199","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said, The Messenger of Allah"
"200","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When one of your servants brings you food"
"201","Abu Mahdhura said, I was sitting with 'Umar when Safwan ibn Umayya brought him a bowl which some people were carrying in a robe. They set it down in front of 'Umar. 'Umar then invited some poor people and some slaves belonging to the people around him and they ate with him. Then he aid"
"202","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When the slave advises his master and is assiduous in the worship of his Lord"
"203","'Three have a double reward: one of the People of the Book who believes in his Prophet and then believes in Muhammad has two rewards. When a slave carries out the due of Allah and the due of his master, he has a double reward. And (the third is) a man who has a slavegirl with whom he has intercourse and teaches her well and instructs her well and then sets her free and marries her. He has two rewards.'""204"""
"204","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The slave who perfects the worship of his Lord and fulfills what is obligatory upon him to his master — obedience and sincere counsel — has two rewards."""
"205","Abu Burda reported from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, The slave has two rewards when he carries out Allah's due in worship (or he said that he is excellent in his worship) and the right of his owner who owns him."""
"206","Ibn 'Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, All of you are shepherds and each of you is responsible for his flock. The amir of a people is a shepherd and he is responsible for his flock. A man is the shepherd of the people of his house and he is responsible for his flock. A man's slave is the shepherd of his master's property and he is responsible for it. Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock."""
"207","Abu Hurayra said, When a slave obeys his master"
"208","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When the Muslim slave performs the due of Allah and the due of his master"
"209","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, None of you should say"
"210","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, None of you should say 'my slave ('abdi or amati)' and a slave should not say"
"211","Mutarrif reported that his father said, I went in the delegation of the Banu 'Amir to the Prophet"
